# allowlist.local.txt.example — template for the OPTIONAL personal provider
# narrowing override (temperloop#1250, ADR 0028 decision 1). This is a
# TRACKED template only; the real file it documents is untracked and lives
# outside this committed subtree, at:
#
#   .temperloop/model-comparison/allowlist.local.txt
#
# (repo-local, gitignored via .temperloop/.gitignore — never a `$HOME`
# config, never an env var: the same repo-scoping ADR 0028 requires for the
# committed ceiling applies to a personal narrowing of it, so a narrowing
# set for one client's checkout can never bleed into another repo's).
#
# Copy this file to that path to use it. Same format as
# provider-allowlist.txt: one lowercase provider name per line, `#` comments
# and blank lines ignored.
#
# RULE: this file may only be a SUBSET of
# workflows/scripts/model-comparison/provider-allowlist.txt's committed
# list. Naming a provider here that the committed file doesn't list is a
# WIDEN attempt — allowlist.sh's pa_effective_list refuses to resolve an
# effective allowlist at all when that happens (fail closed), rather than
# silently granting the extra provider or silently ignoring the bad line.
#
# Example: an operator who never wants ANY non-Anthropic send from this
# checkout, even if the committed file is later widened by a reviewed
# commit, narrows to just:
anthropic
